  "details": "Use an avatar with music. The  audio source range isn't scaled larger to compensate the size change when the avatar is scaled significantly larger than original these audio sources aren't able to be heard or go in and out of range frequently especially dances/emotes.\n\n-------------------------------\n\nHere's my avatar that encounters this issue. I'll make public temporarily. Mostly everything on it is for testing new shaders and other wacky ideas.\n\nAudio source setup:\n\nLinear Rolloff\n\nMin: 0.5\n\nMax: 0.55\n\navtr_46a6d5c7-8562-49d7-87d5-bcb301a0ae11\n\nRadial Menu (R Menu) > Experimental > Synced Emotes\n\nA float parameter for avatar scale could possibly solve the issue but that would require animator setup for the audio sources and/or other objects. If it's possible to automatically scale with avatar scale that would be a lot better.",
